        "type": "the-purpose",
        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "This topic set is designed for a self-learner exploring cosmology with a keen interest in galaxies, but without a formal background in mathematics or advanced science. The primary goal is to bypass complex equations and instead focus on the **conceptual, qualitative, and narrative** aspects of galactic science. These topics explore the \"why\" and \"how\" behind galaxy shapes, the dynamic processes of their growth and interaction, and the profound, symbiotic relationships between their visible and invisible components. The collection emphasizes the \"story\" of galaxies—viewing them as dynamic ecosystems, historical archives, and the fundamental building blocks of the cosmic structure, making the subject both challenging and accessible.",
        "line_number": 27,
        "source": "topic-set-conceptual-guide-to-galactic-structure-🆔20251106223718.md",
        "char_start": 511,
